There will be no fundamental reversal in the future of the social environment in North America and the fact that indigenous brands are more sensitive to customer usage, are more sticky than XCMG and have far higher local research and development inputs than XCMG;
Phenomenal/trend 2: The direction of technological development has shifted from a “triple approach” to an “intelligent priority”
The direction of high-end, smartness has not changed, but the “greening” rhythm has slowed significantly: the Great and Beautiful Act 2025 eliminated most of the federal tax credits for clean energy and electric motorization, and the commercialization of electrical engineering machinery has been significantly reduced; On the contrary, autonomous/semi-autonomous operations, AI-assisted construction and telecommuting are becoming the focus of a new round of competition at the North American mainframe plant — Caterpillar, Komatsu, Volvo etc. have been working with such companies as Built Robotics, SaféAI, Bedrock Robotics and others to introduce commercial products such as autonomous transport and remote excavation;
Case/trend 3: Client bias and lack of understanding of the technical level of XCMG
